.SH "NAME"
lpm.conf \- Lotus Package Manager configuration file
.SS "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
/etc/lpm/lpm.conf
.SS "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
\fIlpm.conf\fP is the single configuration file read by \fBlpm\fP(1). It is a simple
\fIkey = value\fP text file with a fixed key set; lines are \fIkey = value\fP pairs,
\fI#\fP starts a comment to end of line, and blank lines are ignored. Surrounding
single or double quotes around a value are stripped. Both \fIkey=value\fP and
\fIkey = value\fP spacing are accepted, though the canonical Lotus style puts
spaces around \fI=\fP.
.sp
The file is read once, through \fIlpm_config_init()\fP, which populates the
in\-memory config before any command runs. An optional compiler profile is
consulted too (see \fIPROFILE\fP).
.sp
The repository set is \fBnot\fP configured here: \fIlpm\fP fetches from a fixed,
compiled\-in list of repositories (\fIbase\fP, \fIextra\fP, \fIlotus\fP). \fI[base]\fP /
\fI[extra]\fP / \fI[lotus]\fP section headers are \fBnot\fP parsed by the current config
reader and have no effect.
.SS "SYNTAX"
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
# comment
CFLAGS = \-O2 \-pipe
JOBS = 0
CriticalPkg = musl gcc
CriticalPkg = bash coreutils
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
A key appearing on multiple lines is handled per\-key: \fICriticalPkg\fP and
\fIIgnorePkg\fP \fIaccumulate\fP across lines; scalar keys take the last value seen.
.SS "OPTIONS"
.SS "Build environment"
.sp
\fICFLAGS\fP
.RS 4
Type: string. Default: \f(CR\-O2 \-pipe \-fstack\-protector\-strong \-D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=2\fP.
Flags passed to the C compiler during \fIbuild()\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fICXXFLAGS\fP
.RS 4
Type: string. Default: as \fICFLAGS\fP. Flags for the C++ compiler.
.RE
.sp
\fILDFLAGS\fP
.RS 4
Type: string. Default: \f(CR\-Wl,\-z,relro,\-z,now\fP. Flags for the linker.
.RE
.sp
\fIMAKEFLAGS\fP
.RS 4
Type: string. Default: \fI(empty)\fP (the shipped file sets \f(CR\-j4\fP). Extra
flags passed to \fImake\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fICC\fP
.RS 4
Type: string. Default: \fIgcc\fP. C compiler.
.RE
.sp
\fICXX\fP
.RS 4
Type: string. Default: \fIg\f(CR\fP. C\fP compiler.
.RE
.sp
\fIJOBS\fP
.RS 4
Type: integer. Default: \fI0\fP (= automatic, \fInproc\fP). Parallel build jobs.
Negative values are clamped to \fI0\fP.
.RE
.SS "Paths"
.sp
\fIBUILDDIR\fP
.RS 4
Type: path. Default: \fI/var/cache/lpm\fP. Build workspace root.
.RE
.sp
\fIPKGDEST\fP
.RS 4
Type: path. Default: \fI/var/cache/lpm\fP. Where finished package archives go.
.RE
.sp
\fISRCDEST\fP
.RS 4
Type: path. Default: \fI/var/cache/lpm\fP. Downloaded source cache.
.RE
.sp
\fILOGDIR\fP
.RS 4
Type: path. Default: \fI/var/log/lpm\fP. Per\-package build logs. Legacy alias
\fILogDir\fP is also accepted.
.RE
.sp
\fIFILESDIR\fP
.RS 4
Type: path. Default: \fI/var/lib/lpm/files\fP. File\-ownership database root.
Legacy alias \fIFilesDir\fP is also accepted.
.RE
.SS "Download"
.sp
\fIDOWNLOADER\fP
.RS 4
Type: \fIauto\fP, \fIwget\fP, or \fIcurl\fP. Default: \fIauto\fP. \fBauto\fP probes for
\fIwget\fP then \fIcurl\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fIPARALLEL_DL\fP
.RS 4
Type: bool (\fI1\fP/\fI0\fP). Default: \fI1\fP. Download multiple files concurrently.
.RE
.sp
\fIMAX_DL_THREADS\fP
.RS 4
Type: integer, clamped to \fI1\-16\fP. Default: \fI4\fP. Maximum concurrent
download threads when \fIPARALLEL_DL\fP is enabled.
.RE
.sp
\fIVERIFY_SIG\fP
.RS 4
Type: bool. Default: \fI0\fP. When \fI1\fP, verify detached GPG signatures on
repository databases and \fI.lpkg\fP archives (missing or bad signatures
abort with \fISignature verification failed.\fP). When \fI0\fP, a present\-but
invalid signature still fails, but an absent one is tolerated.
.RE
.SS "Build behaviour"
.sp
\fIKEEP_SRC\fP
.RS 4
Type: bool. Default: \fI0\fP. Keep the extracted source tree after a build.
.RE
.sp
\fIKEEP_PKG\fP
.RS 4
Type: bool. Default: \fI0\fP. Keep the staging (pkg) directory after install.
Also controls debug\-symbol stripping of staged files.
.RE
.sp
\fICHECK_SPACE\fP
.RS 4
Type: bool. Default: \fI1\fP. Warn/abort when free disk space is low before a
build or install.
.RE
.sp
\fICOLOR\fP
.RS 4
Type: bool. Default: \fI1\fP. ANSI\-colored terminal output.
.RE
.sp
\fICONFIRM\fP
.RS 4
Type: bool. Accepted by the parser but not present in the shipped file;
interactive confirmation is normally controlled by the \fI\-\-no\-confirm\fP CLI
flag rather than config.
.RE
.sp
\fIPROFILE\fP
.RS 4
Type: string. Default: \fIgeneric\fP. If set, \fIlpm\fP additionally loads
\fI/etc/lpm/profiles/<PROFILE>.conf\fP and applies its keys on top.
.RE
.SS "Package protection"
.sp
\fICriticalPkg\fP
.RS 4
Type: list of names (space\- or comma\-separated, accumulating across
lines). Packages \fIremove\fP refuses to touch without \fI\-\-force\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fIIgnorePkg\fP
.RS 4
Type: list of names (as above). Packages skipped during \fIupgrade\fP.
.RE
.SS "FILES"
.sp
\fI/etc/lpm/lpm.conf\fP
.RS 4
The configuration file.
.RE
.sp
\fI/etc/lpm/profiles/<name>.conf\fP
.RS 4
Optional compiler profile loaded when \fIPROFILE\fP is set.
.RE
.SS "SEE ALSO"
.sp
\fBlpm\fP(1), \fBPKGBUILD\fP(5)